plication in institutionalized settings, such as nursing homes and hospitals. MUST analyzes key factors including Body Mass Index (BMI), weight loss, and the impact of acute illness on food intake to identify individuals who are malnourished or at risk of malnutrition.\n\nThis standardized screening tool is widely utilized in clinical environments and has been specifically noted for its effectiveness in predicting clinical outcomes, including mortality and length of hospital stay, particularly in elderly patients. MUST is recognized for its role in identifying individuals who may require nutritional intervention, especially those preparing for medical procedures like transplants. Developed by the British Association for Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition (BAPEN), MUST serves as an essential resource for healthcare professionals aiming to address malnutrition and improve patient care.\",29\r\n719,FORBES A,\"Forbes A is a prominent author of the ESPEN guidelines on clinical nutrition in inflammatory bowel diseases. Additionally, Forbes A plays a significant role in the international consensus on the diagnosis of malnutrition, contributing to the advancement of nutritional standards and practices in clinical settings.\",2\r\n564,ATENCIÓN PRIMARIA,\"Atención Primaria refers to primary healthcare services that provide initial care and management for patients, including those with diabetes. These services are essential in coordinating with the UFDOF in the Community of Madrid, ensuring comprehensive care for patients. Additionally, Atención Primaria is involved in the management and follow-up of patients receiving home artificial nutrition, playing a key role in the ongoing assessment and management of patients' nutritional status.\",5\r\n13775,PERSONAL SANITARIO,\"El \"\"PERSONAL SANITARIO\"\" se refiere a los profesionales de la salud que operan dentro del Sistema Nacional de Salud. Este grupo incluye médicos y nutricionistas que desempeñan un papel crucial en la evaluación y gestión del estado nutricional de los pacientes, tanto antes como después del trasplante de células hematopoyéticas. Su labor es fundamental para asegurar que los pacientes reciban la atención adecuada y optimicen su recuperación durante este proceso crítico.\",3\r\n717,COMPHER C,\"Compher C is a prominent figure in the field of clinical nutrition, recognized for their significant contributions to various guidelines and proposals aimed at improving patient care. They are a co-author of a proposal focused on etiology-based diagnosis in clinical practice concerning malnutrition, highlighting their commitment to addressing nutritional deficiencies in clinical settings. Additionally, Compher C has contributed to clinical guidelines for nutrition support specifically tailored for hyperglycemic patients, demonstrating their expertise in managing complex nutritional needs. They are also an author of clinical guidelines related to nutrition support in renal failure, further showcasing their involvement in critical areas of patient nutrition management. Furthermore, Compher C has played a key role in authoring the ASPEN clinical guidelines for nutrition screening, which are essential for identifying patients at risk of malnutrition. Lastly, they are one of the authors discussing treatment outcomes of early enteral versus early parenteral nutrition, contributing to the ongoing discourse on optimal nutritional strategies in clinical practice. Overall, Compher C's work reflects a deep commitment to enhancing nutritional support across various patient populations.\",2\r\n1634,EUROPEAN SOCIETY OF PARENTERAL AND ENTERAL NUTRITION,\"The European Society of Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition (ESPEN) is an organization dedicated to advancing research and education in the field of parenteral and enteral nutrition throughout Europe. Its primary focus is on enhancing the quality of nutritional care for patients who require these forms of nutrition. ESPEN plays a crucial role in improving clinical practices by providing guidelines and recommendations that inform healthcare professionals on best practices in nutritional care. Through its efforts, ESPEN aims to support the overall improvement of nutritional practices and outcomes for patients across the continent.\",3\r\n8017,BRITISH ASSOCIATION OF PARENTERAL AND ENTERAL NUTRITION,The British Association of Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition (BAPEN) is an organization that developed the MUST screening tool for malnutrition.,1\r\n718,DHALIWAL R,\"Dhaliwal R is an author who is actively engaged in the systematic review of nutrition support in acute pancreatitis. Additionally, Dhaliwal R contributes to the development of guidelines concerning the diagnosis of malnutrition. Through these efforts, Dhaliwal R plays a significant role in advancing knowledge and practices related to nutrition in clinical settings.\",1\r\n3283,ELIA AND STRATTON,Elia and Stratton are authors who discussed the effectiveness of age in predicting mortality and hospital stay compared to nutritional screening tools.,1\r\n720,FIGUEREDO GRIJALBA R,Figueredo Grijalba R is a contributor to the guidelines for diagnosing malnutrition in clinical settings.,1\r\n563,RESIDENCES DE MAYORES,\"Facilities that provide care for elderly individuals, where nutritional assessments and management are crucial for residents.\",1\r\n716,MIRTALLO J,Mirtallo J is a contributor to the international consensus guidelines on malnutrition.,1\r\n721,NUTRITIONAL RISK SCREENING (NRS2002),Nutritional Risk Screening (NRS2002) is a method developed for assessing nutritional risk based on clinical trials.,1\r\n3286,RAPID SCREEN,\"The Rapid Screen is a quick assessment tool for identifying nutritional risk in various populations, including the elderly.\",1\r\n13774,ONCOLOGY SCREENING TOOL,\"El Oncology Screening Tool (OST) es una herramienta diseñada específicamente para evaluar el estado nutricional de pacientes oncológicos, incluyendo aquellos que se someten a tra